  concept: "Authored objective: Recover safely from sensor loss.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from solved wiring, motor current and measured encoder feedback. voltage
    \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching principle: Sensor outputs
    require proper calibration, reference and freshness before they can support a
    diagnosis.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective
    is complete."
  analogy: A measuring ruler is useful only if zero and units are correctly established.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An old, uncalibrated or missing sensor reading is not reliable evidence.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Recover safely from sensor loss\u2019, which
    component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should
    you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Recover safely from sensor loss\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 47, perform the objective \u2018Recover safely from sensor
    loss\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Recorded
    from solved wiring, motor current and measured encoder feedback. voltage \u2265
    4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this
    tutorial does not grade your answer."
